%language Python

# A name takes the most specific colour that fits it: the one after `def`
# is a function and the one after `class` a type, though every name is
# also an identifier
> class Greeter:
  ^^^^^ keyword
        ^^^^^^^ type
>     def greet(self, name):
      ^^^ keyword
          ^^^^^ function
                ^^^^ variable

# Operators spelt as words are keywords, like `if`
> if not name:
  ^^ keyword
     ^^^ keyword
> for x in xs:
        ^^ keyword

# A builtin is told from any other call; a string, a comment
> return len("hi")  # polite
         ^^^ function.builtin
             ^^^^ string
                    ^^^^^^^^ comment
> greet(x)
  ^^^^^ function

# All capitals is a constant, a capital first a constructor
> MAX = Greeter
  ^^^ constant
        ^^^^^^^ constructor

# A call is a function first, whatever its name looks like
> Greeter()
  ^^^^^^^ function
